TI  - System for generating corrected sentence-case            text, has question-answer named entity recognition            model comprises transformer language model and linear            layer to reduce vector output from transformer model to            two-dimensional vector comprising start position and            end position of brand in text
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a processor for obtaining input                text. The processor generates a set of vectors from                an ensemble of machine-learning models based on the                input text, where the ensemble of models comprises                a pre-trained language model to determine                capitalization for mixed cases and acronyms. A                question-answer named entity recognition (NER)                (QA-NER) model comprises a transformer language                model and a linear layer to reduce a vector output                from the transformer model to a two-dimensional                vector comprising a start position and an end                position of a brand in the text. The corrected                sentence-case text is generated by modifying                capitalization of the text based on vectors.
