TI  - Artificial intelligence-based smart contract            review and loophole warning system has continuous            learning and updating module that is configured to            acquire knowledge once per week from newly issued laws            and regulations and user feedback on results to            incorporate acquired knowledge into model            training
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a warning and modification                suggestion module that is configured to highlight                the problem position of contract in a prominent                color and to pop up a warning prompt with risk                level when a problem is discovered. The targeted                modification suggestions are provided to user, such                that illegal clauses are replaced with standard                clauses compliant with laws and regulations, and                imperfect clauses are supplemented with common                industry solutions. A continuous learning and                updating module is configured to acquire knowledge                once per week from newly issued laws and                regulations, newly emerging typical contract                dispute cases, and user feedback on review results,                to incorporate the acquired knowledge into model                training, thus optimizing model performance and                maintaining the system at industry frontier. The                incremental learning strategy is adopted so as to                avoid large-scale damage to the existing model                structure and parameters and to ensure system                stability.
                    USE - Artificial intelligence-based smart contract                review and loophole warning system.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system is configured such that large and                diverse sets of contract samples are rapidly                integrated through multi-source data acquisition                and efficient preprocessing workflows, and the                latest texts are automatically retrieved in real                time through web crawling to ensure data                timeliness. The text cleaning and structuring                techniques are applied to standardize contracts                into analyzable formats, thus substantially                reducing preliminary preparation time. Machine                learning models are trained with a fusion of                convolutional neural networks (CNN) and recurrent                neural networks (RNN) incorporating attention                mechanisms based on an optimized architecture, thus                enabling rapid extraction of key contract                information. Complex clause analysis, loophole                detection, and risk assessment are completed within                a short period. The detailed review reports can be                provided within minutes, thus greatly increasing                contract processing throughput and meeting the                fast-paced demands of modern commercial operations.                The system is configured such that key entities                within the contract are precisely annotated, and                semantic logic is captured using named entity                recognition and semantic feature extraction                techniques through a refined text feature                enhancement module, thus providing a solid                foundation for risk assessment. The machine                learning model is trained on a large dataset of                diverse contract types and optimized using                cross-validation and early stopping methods, such                that excellent generalization capability is                achieved. Thus, various clause loopholes are                accurately identified, including defects in payment                or delivery terms, potential risks such as                imbalanced rights or improperly scoped                confidentiality clauses. The real-time comparison                against a daily-updated legal and regulatory                database allows illegal clausessuch as violations                of penalty provisions or exclusion of liability                terms to be precisely detected, thus effectively                preventing hidden contractual risks from causing                significant losses to enterprises. The system is                configured such that a continuous learning and                updating module plays a key role, with knowledge                acquired from multiple sources. Legal news crawlers                track legislative developments daily, cooperation                with professional institutions introduces the                latest case data, and user feedback is continuously                incorporated, thus constantly accumulating new                knowledge. The new data is integrated to train the                model, with weighted learning applied to new                regulations and emerging risk features, without                disrupting existing model parameters, thus allowing                the system to rapidly adapt to changes. The system                is prevented from becoming outdated due to legal                amendments, newly emerging contract types, or                specific user requirements, and is maintained in a                state that continuously meets the forefront                requirements of contract review. High-quality and                practical review services are persistently                provided, thus safeguarding the long-term stability                of business operations.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram                illustrating the artificial intelligence-based                contract smart review and loophole warning system.                (Drawing includes non-English language text)
