TI  - Intelligent auditing method for government data,            involves allowing to-be-issued government text or            finishing modified government text to be issued and            issuing operation
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves receiving a pre-collected                prohibiting issuing text set (S1), where the                prohibiting issuing texts include sensitive                entities. Structural government affair phrase is                input (S2) to a name entity. A word vector is used                (S3) to convert structured government affair phrase                into structured government affair vector set. A                first feature extraction layer is used (S4) to                perform first feature extraction. Second feature                extraction layer is used (S5) to perform second                feature extraction. The name recognition prediction                layer is used (S6) to predict the naming entity of                each government affair characteristic in the second                government affair matrix set. The named entity                recognition set is obtained. The intelligent                auditing is performed (S7) to the named entity                identification set to obtain the audit result                whether to allow issuing. The editor is reminded to                re-modify the government text to be issued.
                    USE - Intelligent auditing method for government                data.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables removing sensitive words,                so as to reduce the consumption of human resource                waste caused by overly relying on manual review of                government data. The problem that manual auditing                government data caused by manpower resource waste                can be solved, by performing intelligent auditing                to the named entity identification set to obtain                the audit result whether to allow issuing.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a                government affair data intelligent auditing                device.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flowchart illustrating an                intelligent auditing method for government data                (Drawing includes non-English language                text).S1Step for receiving a pre-collected                prohibiting issuing text setS2Step for inputting structural government                affair phrase to a name entityS3Step for using word vector to convert                structured government affair phrase into structured                government affair vector setS4Step for using first feature extraction                layer to perform first feature extractionS5Step for using second feature extraction                layer to perform second feature extractionS6Step for using name recognition prediction                layer to predict the naming entity of each                government affair characteristic in the second                government affair matrix setS7Step for performing intelligent auditing to                the named entity identification set to obtain the                audit result whether to allow issuing
