TI  - System for detecting fraudulent or illicit            activity in peer-to-peer transactions using natural            language processing using e.g. tablet computer, has            each processor for triggering remediation action for            P2P transaction based on textual information
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has multiple processors (420)                communicatively coupled to multiple memories (430).                Each processor obtains information associated with                indicators related to fraudulent or illicit                activity in peer-to-peer (P2P) transactions,                receives textual information related to a P2P                transaction between a sending user and a receiving                user, analyzes the textual information related to                the P2P transaction using natural language                processing (NLP) to determine whether the P2P                transaction includes the indicators related to                fraudulent or illicit activity. Each processor                triggers a remediation action for the P2P                transaction based on the textual information                including the indicators related to fraudulent or                illicit activity.
                    USE - System for detecting fraudulent or illicit                activity in P2P transactions using natural language                processing (NLP) using a computing device. Uses                include but are not limited to computing device                such as wireless communication device, a mobile                phone, a user equipment, a laptop computer, a                tablet computer, a desktop computer, a wearable                communication device e.g. a smart wristwatch, a                pair of smart eyeglasses, a head mounted display,                or a virtual reality headset, or a similar type of                device.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system improves accuracy of fraud and/or                illegal behavior detection, polarity detection to                assess whether a sentiment expressed in the text                accompanying the P2P transaction is positive,                negative, or neutral, and emotion detection to                identify specific emotions such as anger, fear, or                excitement that can be indicative of fraud, and                named entity recognition (NER) to identify and                categorize entities such as names, dates, amounts,                and organizations and detect unusual patterns, such                as mismatched names or unexpected organizations.                The system triggers a risk assessment workflow,                where the P2P transaction is manually or                automatically reviewed to further assess the risk                of fraud, illicit behavior, or abusive                behavior.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for:(1) a method for assessing a risk of                fraudulent or illicit activity in P2P                transactions;(2) a non-transitory computer-readable medium                storing a set of instructions for assessing a risk                of fraudulent or illicit activity in P2P                transactions.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a device                for detecting fraudulent or illicit activity in P2P                transactions.420Processors430Memories440Input component450Output component460Communication component
