TI  - Public data sources for regulatory genomic features
T2  - MEDIZINISCHE GENETIK
M3  - Article
AB  - High-throughput technologies have led to a continuously growing amount of information about regulatory features in the genome. A wealth of data generated by large international research consortia is available from online databases. Disease-driven studies provide details on specific DNA elements or epigenetic modifications regulating gene expression in specific cellular and developmental contexts, but these results are usually only published in scientific articles. All this information can be helpful in interpreting variants in the regulatory genome. This review describes a selection of high-profile data sources providing information on the non-coding genome, as well as pitfalls and techniques to search and capture information from the literature.
