TI  - Social Recognition and Requirements for Establishing Standardization Governance: An Analysis of Social Recognition in Online News Articles
TI  - 표준화 거버넌스 구축을 위한 사회적 인식과 요건: 온라인 뉴스 기사에 나타난 표준 관련 인식에 대한 분석
T2  - Korean Public Management Review
T2  - 한국공공관리학보
M3  - research-article
AB  - The study aims to extract key stakeholders, technologies, products, etc. using a Named Entity Recognition technique and to examine the changes in the recognition of standardization governance utilizing the network analysis methods by surveying online news about standardization. Therefore, by separating articles including the main concepts of standardization governance ㅡ mediation or innovation, regulation or deregulation, and diversity or uniformity ㅡ and by analyzing detailed key words for each article, the status and level of the social recognition for standardization governance were reviewed and identified. The study found that the government and major ministries were at the forefront, which means the government-led standardization activities. And the National Assembly and major political parties played the main role in the regulation. The auto industry was the most frequent in the industry and followed by IoT and electric cars which are the leading industries of the fourth industrial revolution. In the main concepts of standardization governance, mediation, innovation and regulation were frequently used. Consequently, the standardization is both the object and means of mediation and innovation, and the regulation was recognized as their method. Although the standards have been widespread in diverse areas, the governance through participation of stakeholders is not sufficient. Therefore, the governance should be achieved through the participation of stakeholders in private sector and the democratic coordination and mediation.
