AU  - Karthika, S. K.
AU  - Mubeen, Noorul
TI  - MCRAH-GIE: Multidimensional contextual retrieval with adaptive hierarchical gap impact embedding generation
T2  - RESULTS IN ENGINEERING
M3  - Article
AB  - In the present scenario manual exhaustive scientific literature research and existing research analysis approaches that are based on Artificial Intelligence struggle in research gap identifications and gap forecasting due to lack of huge scientific corpora, semantic understanding and limited scientific vocabulary. The proposed approach termed as MCRAH-GIE (Multidimensional Contextual Retrieval with Adaptive Hierarchical Gap Impact Embedding Generation) provides an efficient approach for automated in-depth research literature analysis. This architecture makes use of a novel semantic chunking termed as 'Triadic Chunking' using fine-tuned intent classification that achieves 96% accuracy. It also uses hierarchical embeddings for nuanced semantic understanding, multi-tier gap validation and knowledge graph construction with efficient memory utilization in order to support systems with limited resources. MCRAH-GIE paves way to five new use cases which include visualizations and detailed reporting on gap-impact feasibility matrices , gap forecast mapping to predict the future advancements on solving a gap, methodology evolution tracking that maps the complete flow of ideas emerged and advanced till date, claim evidence reconciliation mapping to provide researchers with supporting or contradicting evidences to their claim and peer review vulnerability shields to aid researchers by indicating the vulnerable areas in their literature.
