AU  - Zhang, Yan
AU  - Du, Yuanhao
AU  - Li, Dan
TI  - A novel methodological framework for evaluating and optimizing PSS solutions based on user reviews and intelligent technologies
T2  - ADVANCED ENGINEERING INFORMATICS
M3  - Article
AB  - With the trend of servitization in manufacturing, the product-service system (PSS) has become a popular business paradigm because of the achievement in value co-creation between multiple stakeholders. Owing to the important role of users, requirements of sustainability, and the explosion of online data, leveraging intelligent technologies to efficiently exploit user reviews and empower PSS solution evaluation and optimization becomes a significant research question. Most existing evaluation methods based on user reviews rely heavily on term frequency, failing to understand the demand deeply hidden in the semantic association. Additionally, the current optimization is often achieved by manual analysis for evaluation results in the form of linguistic or text sentences, which is too vague and unintelligent to guide the efficient solution improvement. Accordingly, this paper proposes a novel methodological framework for evaluating and optimizing PSS solutions based on user reviews and intelligent technologies. To address the absence of labeled training datasets for extracting evaluation indicators, an automatic annotation technology based on Sentence-BERT model is introduced, which prevents the high cost of manual annotation. Furthermore, to deeply understand demands hidden in semantics of user reviews, a graph-based semantic analysis approach is proposed, which contributes to the indicator importance calculation. Then, importance-performance analysis is applied to identify indicators urgent to optimize, and the theory of inventive problem solving (TRIZ) is adopted to propose optimization strategies. A Stable Diffusion graph generation model is employed to present the enhanced PSS solution intuitively and intelligently. Finally, a case study involving a Van-PSS is conducted to validate the proposed framework, with experimental comparisons and in-depth analysis demonstrating its effectiveness and reliability.
